==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|allodial}}, and its source, {{der|en|la|allodialis||held in freehold}}, from {{m|la|allodium}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈləʊdiəl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-allodial.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|usually|historical}} Pertaining to [[land]] owned by someone [[absolutely]], without any [[feudal]] obligations; held without acknowledgement of any superior; [[allodial title]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author={{w|Peter H. Wilson}}|title=The Holy Roman Empire|page=351|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2017
|passage=Henry reconciled the Zähringer, whom he had deposed from Carinthia in 1078, by raising their '''allodial''' property in the Black Forest to a new duchy 20 years later.}}

